#include <stdio.h>
int main(void){puts("ECB/CBC error propagation: conceptual lab");puts("a) CBC ciphertext bit error in C1: P1 is corrupted unpredictably; the corresponding bit in P2 flips. Blocks P3 onward are not affected by that ciphertext error.");puts("b) A bit error in source plaintext P1 changes C1 and therefore affects every later CBC ciphertext block (because each block depends on the previous ciphertext). At the receiver, the resulting message differs from P1 onward; the precise changes depend on the block cipher.");puts("ECB differs: a damaged ciphertext block generally damages only its matching plaintext block.");return 0;}
